---
description: Rules for editing package source, tests and changesets
globs:
  - "packages/**"
  - ".changeset/**"
alwaysApply: false
---

- A change to a module needs a changeset: `.changeset/<kebab-slug>.md` with the shim's
  `package.json` name (`readthrough`, `readthrough-prom`) and `patch` / `minor` / `major`.
  While a module is 0.x a breaking change is `minor`, and the text must say so. A README-only
  change needs none.
- After writing a changeset by hand run `node .github/scripts/sync-changeset-ignore.mjs --write`.
- Never add an observability dependency to `packages/readthrough`; Prometheus code goes in
  `packages/readthrough/prom`.
- Behaviour changes need the README updated and tests in the same change.
- Build and test as a consumer would: `GOWORK=off go build ./... && GOWORK=off go vet ./...`
  inside the module (this needs required versions to be tagged).
- Full procedure: `.ai/skills/commit-strategy/SKILL.md`.
